@startuml lakehouse-flight-v1-sequence
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam participant {
  BorderColor #534AB7
  BackgroundColor #EEEDFE
  FontColor #26215C
}
skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #993C1D
  BackgroundColor #FAECE7
  FontColor #4A1B0C
}

title delta-flight-engine v1 — Query Round Trip\nCopyright 2026 Afzal and lakehouse-flight contributors — Apache 2.0

actor       "Client\n(Python / Java / lakehouse-gateway)" as C
participant "DeltaFlightProducer"                          as DFP
participant "TableLocation\n+ TableCache"                   as TL
participant "SnapshotManager"                               as SM
participant "QueryPlanner"                                  as QP
participant "TicketRegistry"                                as TR
participant "ParquetToArrowReader"                          as PTAR

== Optional: GetSchema (cheap schema discovery, no scan) ==

C   -> DFP  : GetSchema(FlightDescriptor)\n{"table":"logs"}
DFP -> TL   : resolveTableRoot → TableLocation\n(local path or s3a:// or abfss://)
DFP -> SM   : TableCache.forTable() → latest snapshot
DFP -> PTAR : readSchema(firstFile, partitionValues)\n(opens one file footer only, cached)
DFP --> C   : SchemaResult\n(column names + types, used by NL validator)

== Phase 1: GetFlightInfo (planning — no data files fully opened) ==

C   -> DFP  : GetFlightInfo(FlightDescriptor)\n{"table":"logs","predicate":{...},"columns":[...]}
DFP -> TL   : resolveTableRoot → TableLocation
DFP -> SM   : TableCache.forTable() → SnapshotManager

group Snapshot resolution (log/ layer)
  SM  -> SM  : find latest checkpoint ≤ version\n(single-part or multi-part — all parts verified + merged)
  SM  -> SM  : replay JSON commits from checkpoint → version\n(incremental: only new commits applied on cache hit)
  SM  --> DFP : Snapshot (live file set + schema + partition columns)
end

DFP -> QP   : plan(snapshot, predicate, columns)

group Pruning — Layer 2 (no file opened yet)
  QP  -> QP  : ① PartitionPruner\n   exact match on partition values from log\n   supports = != IN LIKE AND OR
  QP  -> QP  : ② FileStatsPruner\n   range check on add.stats min/max from log\n   IN gets real range pruning; LIKE fails open
  QP  -> QP  : PredicateColumns.collect()\n   ensures predicate cols included in physical read set\n   (fixes projection + predicate bug)
  QP  --> DFP : ScanPlan (surviving files only + files-skipped metric)
end

loop for each surviving file
  DFP -> DFP  : PartitionValueSubstituter\n  fold "level=ERROR AND amount>2" → "amount>2"\n  (partition clause resolved to constant, safe for decode)
  DFP -> TR   : register(ScanTicket)\n  carries: TableLocation · projectedColumns · residual predicate · partitionValues
  TR  --> DFP : opaque ticket id
end

DFP --> C   : FlightInfo\n  schema + N FlightEndpoints (one per surviving file)\n  client can fetch endpoints in parallel

== Phase 2: DoGet (one per endpoint, can run in parallel) ==

C   -> DFP  : DoGet(ticket)
DFP -> TR   : lookup(ticketId) → ScanTicket
TR  --> DFP : ScanTicket (TableLocation + columns + residual predicate)

DFP -> PTAR : read(dataFile, allocator, columns, residualPredicate, partitionValues)\ndataFile is TableLocation — dispatches local File or Hadoop InputFile

group Decode — Layer 3 (file now opened)
  PTAR -> PTAR : open via ParquetInputFiles\n  (local: java.io.File · remote: HadoopInputFile for s3a/abfss)
  PTAR -> PTAR : read footer (schema + row-group metadata)
  PTAR -> PTAR : ③ RowGroupPruner\n   range check on Parquet footer stats\n   skipNextRowGroup() for pruned ones
  loop for each surviving row group
    PTAR -> PTAR : decode projected columns only\n  (unrequested column bytes never read off disk)
    PTAR -> PTAR : nested LIST columns → NestedTypeDecoder\n  (LIST<float/double/int/string> for embedding vectors)
    PTAR -> PTAR : INT96 timestamps → Int96TimestampCodec\n  (epoch-micros → Instant, UTC, no rebasing)
    PTAR -> PTAR : ④ GroupPredicateEvaluator\n   per-row residual filter (fused with decode)\n   failing rows never enter Arrow vectors
    PTAR -> PTAR : PartitionValueAppender\n   fill level/log_date as constants\n   (not in physical Parquet file — from folder name)
  end
end

PTAR --> DFP : VectorSchemaRoot (predicate-only cols stripped from output)
DFP --> C   : Arrow IPC stream\n(zero-copy — Flight wire format IS Arrow IPC)
DFP -> TR   : invalidate(ticketId)

note over C, DFP
  Pruning levels — in order of cheapness:
  ① partition values    from _delta_log,  no file I/O
  ② file stats min/max  from _delta_log,  no file I/O
  ③ row-group stats     Parquet footer,   one file open (header only)
  ④ per-row residual    fused with decode, zero wasted materialisation

  Storage dispatch (TableLocation):
  local path   → java.nio.file / java.io.File
  s3a://       → HadoopLogStorage + ParquetInputFiles (hadoop-aws)
  abfss://     → HadoopLogStorage + ParquetInputFiles (hadoop-azure)
  Credentials via MinioConfiguration / AdlsConfiguration or env vars
end note

@enduml
